* Technical concepts\nbehind the 2019 hacks
** Was the deposit real?
*** XRP partial payments (delivered_amount)
*** EOS: fake EOS, fake notifications
*** EOS hard_fail status, Tron fake token ID
** Randomness and atomicity
*** Predictable seeds (tapos, block id)
*** Deferred-transaction congestion
*** Rollback by assert, blacklist rollback
** Exchange controls
*** API keys and 2FA codes (Binance)
*** Review processes (Bitrue)
*** Hot-wallet keys (Upbit, BITPoint)
** Ethereum near-misses
*** Return data from a call to an EOA (0x v2)
*** Oracle with too few sources (Synthetix)
*** ERC-777 reentrancy warning (Uniswap v1)
** Below the contracts
*** 51% reorganisations (ETC, Vertcoin)
*** Signature verification bug (NULS)
*** Supply chain (npm, Electrum, browser scripts)
@endmindmap
